<%- include('partials/header', {title: 'Cognito Authentication & Authorization'}) %>

<section class="project-hero">
  <a href="/" class="project-back-btn"><i class="fas fa-arrow-left"></i> Back to Portfolio</a>
  <h1>Cognito Authentication & Authorization</h1>
  <p>Secured a Birds web application using Amazon Cognito — user pool authentication for protected pages and identity pool authorization for DynamoDB access.</p>
  <div class="project-hero-tags">
    <span>Cognito</span><span>User Pool</span><span>Identity Pool</span><span>DynamoDB</span><span>IAM</span><span>Authentication</span>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="project-details">
  <div class="center">
    <img src="/images/cognito-auth.png" alt="Cognito Authentication Architecture" class="project-diagram">
  </div>

  <div class="project-section">
    <h3>Project Overview</h3>
    <p>This project demonstrates <strong>complete authentication and authorization</strong> using Amazon Cognito for a web application with protected pages and database access control.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Created a <strong>Cognito User Pool</strong> for user authentication.</li>
      <li>Integrated <strong>Cognito Managed UI</strong> with the Birds Node.js application.</li>
      <li>Created a <strong>Cognito Identity Pool</strong> for AWS service authorization.</li>
      <li>Configured <strong>IAM roles</strong> for DynamoDB access with temporary credentials.</li>
      <li>Implemented <strong>role-based access control</strong> (student vs admin).</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="project-section alt-bg">
    <h3>Architecture Explanation</h3>
    <div class="architecture-grid">
      <div class="arch-component">
        <h4>🔐 Authentication</h4>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Cognito User Pool</strong> — User management</li>
          <li><strong>Managed UI</strong> — Sign-up/sign-in flow</li>
          <li><strong>Access tokens</strong> — Stored in browser (3,600s)</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="arch-component">
        <h4>🔑 Authorization</h4>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Identity Pool</strong> — Exchanges tokens for AWS creds</li>
          <li><strong>IAM Roles</strong> — DynamoDB scoped permissions</li>
          <li>Temporary credentials for each user</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="arch-component">
        <h4>🌐 Application</h4>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Cloud9</strong> — Hosts Node.js app</li>
          <li><strong>S3 + CloudFront</strong> — Static content delivery</li>
          <li><strong>DynamoDB</strong> — Bird sightings data</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="project-section">
    <h3>Implementation Steps</h3>
    <div class="steps-grid">
      <div class="step-item"><div class="step-num">1</div><p>Created <strong>Cognito User Pool</strong> with sign-up/sign-in configuration.</p></div>
      <div class="step-item"><div class="step-num">2</div><p>Configured <strong>App Client</strong> and integrated Cognito SDK into Node.js app.</p></div>
      <div class="step-item"><div class="step-num">3</div><p>Protected pages (sightings, reporting, admin) — require <strong>token validation</strong>.</p></div>
      <div class="step-item"><div class="step-num">4</div><p>Created <strong>Identity Pool</strong> and configured IAM roles with DynamoDB permissions.</p></div>
      <div class="step-item"><div class="step-num">5</div><p>Updated admin page to query DynamoDB using <strong>temporary AWS credentials</strong>.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="project-section alt-bg">
    <h3>Key Learnings</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Used <strong>User Pools</strong> for authentication and <strong>Identity Pools</strong> for authorization.</li>
      <li>Exchanged <strong>tokens for temporary AWS credentials</strong> via Identity Pool.</li>
      <li>Implemented <strong>role-based access control</strong> (student vs admin).</li>
      <li>Secured <strong>DynamoDB queries</strong> with scoped Cognito authorization.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="center">
    <a href="/" class="btn-back"><i class="fas fa-arrow-left"></i> Back to Portfolio</a>
  </div>
</div>

